this is a production of cornell  university  hello my name is carl scamenti from the  cornell turf grass program  and today i'm going to go through a  really quick tutorial on how to use the  web soil survey  this online free tool that gives you a  lot of information about the soils at  your property  really quickly so you know first thing  just type in  in google web soil survey you'll find  this page  and if you want to read more about the  you know the data that goes into the web  solar survey how they did it you can but  um easiest way to do it is just click  the green button to get started  and you'll get right to the online tools  so a lot of things kind of going on in  this website but  the best way to start is just to put in  the address of  the site you're interested in today  we're just going to use the robert trent  jones golf course  at cornell um  i could put in the exact address but  instead i'll just type in a  name of the golf course and that gets me  at least in tompkins county now i'm just  using the zoom in zoom out feature  to find our golf course here now we're  zeroing in on it  there we go so here's robert jones golf  course  so now okay what do i do i have to draw  my boundary around  the area i'm interested in so we see  these uh  shapes aoi that means area of interest  i'm going to click on this one which  will just allow me to  basically draw a boundary of the area  so i'm just going to circle our front  line here at cornell  and then uh kind of a little tricky  thing here doesn't really explain it but  you have to double click  to kind of confirm this and there we go  it created our area of interest  and and that's pretty easy now we can go  in and look at a bunch of  information on our soils the first thing  you can do is just click soil map  and here we go generates a pretty  detailed map right you can see of the  soils at your golf course  has all the information it's got the  corresponding map unit  uh sandy loam gravely loan right silty  clay loam  uh and then a cool little aspect is is  the percentage of the property that is  that soil type two so already i see  almost fifty percent is this  hudson silty clay loam that's  interesting  um and so then you can kind of go a  little bit deeper  actually a lot deeper and you can look  at all the information in the soil data  explorer  i like to go to the soil properties and  qualities area and really kind of  investigate all of the things that you  can look at  there's a lot of information here right  chemical properties  soil health soil physical properties i  like to go to  the drainage class which is under soil  qualities and features right here  so when you go into any one of these  selections  you can just go ahead and view the  rating and it spits out that map again  now it color codes it  based on the drainage class so when i  scroll down  i can look at my soils i look at  what they're rated right so we see some  poorly drained somewhat poorly drained  soils  these rhinebeck silk loams make up over  20 percent of the property  so then we can go up we can look at rka  rkb  where does that correspond on the map  okay we look at some really  kind of very specific areas that have  these soil types  and that might correspond to things  you've seen on the property before  the composition of the turf grass  species in that area  those are probably going to be wetter  areas if you ever noticed them before  this might help you target maybe soil  sampling  or drainage installation so certainly  some information here that might  correspond to patterns you've seen in  the past  but could also be really useful for  things you want to do in the future so  that's just one of you know literally  hundreds of things you can  go looking for in this web soil survey  again it's free pretty easy to use once  you once you do it once or twice  and then if you want to kind of print  all this stuff out  they have this shopping cart here tab uh  in the top right you can just click  check out and  what that'll do i've already got my  little report here  it'll generate a report for you so this  is what it looks like  you can scroll through this uh one of  the nice parts is it will make a map for  you so i think it's always useful for  someone to have the  soil map just just as a print out in the  office in the maintenance area  so everybody can kind of see what's  what's going on out there if they notice  things  you can start keeping notes and seeing  if um certain turf grass issues  correspond to also the soil issues  out on the property uh and then of  course there's a bunch of information  about each soil type so you can have  this in a  in a binder if you want in your office  um so that's web show  survey um you know a note for newer golf  courses where there's been a significant  amount of soil moved  ground move to create the golf course  this data depending on when it was taken  may not be super representative after  you've disturbed  the area like that but for older golf  courses a really great tool  uh to give some insight on your property  thanks for watching see you next time  this has been a production of cornell  university  on the web at cornell.edu
 

